  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1003 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe long term forecast looks rather benign, aside from chilly\nmornings near freezing. Residual CAA will continue to cool\ntemperatures during the day through the weekend, bottoming out\naround 60 degrees Sunday afternoon. After that, a more dominant\nridging pattern begins to emerge and afternoon temperatures begin\na very slow climb back upwards. However, large scale high \npressure will be sitting over the Lower MS River Valley this \nweekend into early next week, which will promote efficient \nradiational cooling overnight. This will result in temperatures in\nthe low to mid 30s starting Saturday and continuing through at \nleast Tuesday morning. The coldest morning looks to be Monday with\nseveral locations on the Plateau reading in the upper 20s.",
